  "question": {
    "text": "A stone of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is tied to a string and moved in a vertical circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> making <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>rpm</mi></math>. The tension in the string, when the stone is at the lowest point is (if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
